    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/Department-Head--Department-of-Microbiology--Immunology--and-Pathology_R2026107462": {
      "title": "Department Head, Department of Microbiology, Immunology, and Pathology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\nJob Description Colorado State University: Colorado State University (CSU) is Colorado’s land-grant university and a Carnegie R1 research institution. CSU advances teaching, research, engagement, and service for the benefit of Colorado, the nation, and the world. Located in Fort Collins, CSU offers a highly collaborative environment for interdisciplinary scholarship and education, with broad strengths in the life sciences, veterinary medicine, public health, agriculture, engineering, data science, and environmental sustainability.  College of Veterinary Medicine and Biomedical Sciences: The CSU land grant mission is dedicated to education, research, service, and outreach which permeates the college. CVMBS’ vision is to advance the well-being of animals, people, and the planet. CVMBS offers undergraduate, professional, and graduate courses of study, and confers Doctor of Veterinary Medicine, Master of Science and Doctor of Philosophy degrees in a range of biomedical and veterinary medical topic areas. The College is comprised of four departments: Biomedical Sciences; Clinical Sciences; Environmental Health and Radiological Sciences; and Microbiology, Immunology, and Pathology. CVMBS is fully accredited by the American Veterinary Medical Association, and has been highly ranked in national surveys, including U.S. News & World Report, Blue Ridge Institute, and Planetary Health Report Card. CVMBS faculty explore a variety of pivotal issues in human and animal health via world-renowned research programs in infectious disease, orthopedics, neuroscience, cancer biology, animal reproduction, and translational medicine, with annual extramural funding in the range of $60-100M. CVMBS has created the Veterinary Health System (VHS) to provide oversight management of operations of four clinical units and the state diagnostic laboratory to provide a collective and efficient approach to patient care delivered with the highest level of customer service, employee satisfaction, and advancements in medicine.  Department of Microbiology, Immunology, and Pathology: The Department of Microbiology, Immunology, and Pathology (MIP) comprises more than 80 faculty, and over 400 staff, trainees, and students united by a commitment to addressing consequential problems in animal and human health. MIP is a broad, interdisciplinary department with missions in discovery, education, clinical and diagnostic services, and engagement. With greater than 90 faculty, expertise spans anatomic and clinical pathology, bacteriology, cancer biology, clinical diagnostics, computational biology, genomics, immunology, microbiomes, mycobacterial diseases, parasitology, prion biology, RNA biology, science pedagogy, scientific communication, vector biology, and virology.  The department contributes to undergraduate and graduate education, the Doctor of Veterinary Medicine program, residency and advanced clinical training, and instruction for students at the University of Colorado School of Medicine program at CSU. MIP is intricately connected with the Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratories, the VHS, and the One Health Institute, and includes major research enterprises such as the Center for Vector-Borne Infectious Diseases, Mycobacteria Research Laboratories, and the Prion Research Center. This breadth along with a presence on all three CSU campuses in Fort Collins creates exceptional opportunities for collaboration across basic science, clinical medicine, diagnostics, public health, and One Health research. More information about the department is available in the Department Head Prospectus . Position Summary: CVMBS invites applications and nominations for the position of Head of the Department of Microbiology, Immunology, and Pathology. The Department Head will provide strategic, academic, scientific, administrative, and cultural leadership for a large and highly interdisciplinary department. The successful candidate will articulate an ambitious and inclusive vision; foster excellence across research, education, diagnostic and clinical service, and engagement; steward human, financial, and physical resources; and create conditions in which faculty, staff, and trainees can thrive.  The Department Head reports to the Dean of CVMBS and serves as a member of the College’s senior leadership team. The Head will work in close partnership with MIP associate department heads, center and program directors, the department administrative team, other academic department heads, the Veterinary Health System, and the leadership of the Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratories. The Head will represent and advocate for MIP within CSU and with external academic, government, industry, philanthropic, and community partners.  Full Consideration Date: please apply by Sunday, 10/25/2026, 11:59pm (MT). Review of applications will begin on 10/26/2026 and continue until the position is filled. Salary: $250,000-$300,000; signing bonus possible. Leadership Opportunities and Priorities: Engage the MIP community in developing and implementing a forward-looking strategic vision that builds on established strengths while identifying emerging opportunities in research, education, diagnostics, service, and engagement.  Advance a supportive, accountable, and collaborative organizational culture grounded in the CSU Principles of Community and the CVMBS values of community, integrity, collaboration, and innovation.  Develop and mentor faculty and staff across career stages; promote transparent workload, evaluation, promotion, recognition, and succession practices; and cultivate future leaders.  Enhance educational excellence and integration across undergraduate, graduate, professional, residency, and medical curricula, while supporting innovation in teaching and trainee development.  Strengthen the department’s research portfolio by supporting faculty success, facilitating interdisciplinary and team science, recruiting strategically, and expanding partnerships and resources for discovery and translation.  Partner with the Veterinary Health System and Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratories to sustain and advance high-quality diagnostic, clinical, and service programs and to strengthen connections among diagnostics, research, and education.  Ensure responsible financial and operational stewardship, including strategic budgeting, space and infrastructure planning, research support, administrative effectiveness, and risk management.  Increase the visibility, influence, and external engagement of MIP and communicate the department’s contributions to animal health, human health, public health, and scientific discovery.  Position the department for its next era of growth by expanding student and trainee recruitment and educational opportunities while cultivating innovative, and diversified sources of support for its research portfolio.  Required Qualifications: Ph.D., D.V.M., M.D., or equivalent terminal degree in a discipline relevant to the department.  A record of scholarly achievement and professional distinction that merits appointment as Professor with tenure in the Department of Microbiology, Immunology, and Pathology.  Demonstrated leadership experience in an academic, research, clinical, diagnostic, governmental, or comparably complex organization.  Evidence of effective administrative, personnel, and fiscal management.  A sustained commitment to excellence in research, education, service, and professional development.  Preferred Qualifications and Leadership Attributes: A compelling record of inclusive, transparent, and collaborative leadership, including the ability to build trust, establish clear expectations, make timely decisions, and promote accountability.  Ability to develop and communicate an inspiring vision and translate that vision into coherent strategy, measurable priorities, and effective execution.  Demonstrated success recruiting, retaining, developing, mentoring, and evaluating faculty and staff across varied roles and career stages.  A strong record of advancing a positive academic culture that supports belonging, accessibility, professional respect, constructive dialogue, and the success of individuals with varied backgrounds and perspectives.  Outstanding interpersonal, written, oral, and listening skills, with the capacity to communicate effectively across disciplinary and professional communities.  A record of integrity, sound judgment, courage, fairness, and respect in complex decision-making in a changing environment.  Experience leading externally funded research and an understanding of the infrastructure, compliance, facilities, and administrative systems needed for a high-performing research enterprise.  Experience with undergraduate, graduate, professional, residency, or medical education and a commitment to educational innovation and student success.  Experience with or understanding of diagnostic or clinical service environments and the opportunities created by integrating service, education, and research.  Demonstrated success building productive collaborations across departments, colleges, universities, government, industry, foundations, alumni, donors, and community partners.  Ability to advocate effectively for the department within and beyond CSU to enhance the visibility and reputation of its disciplines and programs.  Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Department Leadership and Administration — approximately 75% : Provide strategic leadership for all departmental missions and guide the development, implementation, assessment, and renewal of departmental priorities.  Serve as the chief administrative and academic officer of the department and represent MIP on the CVMBS leadership team and in university governance and planning.  Lead faculty and staff recruitment, onboarding, retention, annual evaluation, workload planning, recognition, professional development, promotion, and succession planning in accordance with university and college policies.  Build and sustain an environment characterized by collegiality, collaboration, accountability, effective communication, and shared commitment to excellence.  Oversee departmental financial planning and management, including annual budgets, commitments, resource allocation, revenue-generating activities, and long-range financial strategy.  Partner with the department's administrative team to ensure effective operations, internal controls, compliance, and administrative support for departmental missions.  Advocate for and oversee the strategic use, acquisition, renovation, and maintenance of space, equipment, and research and teaching infrastructure.  Support faculty in securing extramural funding, developing interdisciplinary initiatives, and strengthening core capabilities and shared research resources.  Ensure effective mentoring structures for faculty, staff, and trainees and address barriers to professional growth and organizational effectiveness.  Work collaboratively with the Veterinary Health System and Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratories leadership on faculty roles, service priorities, program quality, resource planning, and integration of diagnostic missions with education and research.  Cultivate relationships with alumni, donors, foundations, government agencies, industry, professional organizations, and other external partners in collaboration with College and University leadership.  Model the highest standards of ethical conduct, stewardship, safety, compliance, and professional responsibility.  Scholarly, Educational, Clinical, or Diagnostic Activity — approximately 25% :  Maintain an appropriate program of scholarly, educational, clinical, diagnostic, or professional activity consistent with the candidate’s expertise and the expectations of a tenured Professor.  Contribute to the intellectual life and educational mission of the department and College through teaching, mentoring, research, clinical or diagnostic service, or related professional engagement.  Conditions of Employment: Pre-employment criminal background check (required for new hires). Application Materials: Applicants should submit the following through the CSU Jobs website . Applications will not be considered complete until all listed documents have been submitted:  A cover letter describing the candidate’s interest in the position and experience relevant to the responsibilities and qualifications.  A curriculum vitae.  A statement of leadership and administrative philosophy, including examples of leading people and organizations through change and opportunity.  A vision statement describing priorities for advancing MIP’s research, education, diagnostic and clinical service, organizational culture, and external impact.  Names and contact information for three professional references. References will not be contacted without prior notification to the candidate.  Appointment and Search Information: This is a 12-month, full-time, tenured faculty position to begin in spring or summer 2027. Salary and start-up support will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. For questions about the position, contact Dr. Gregg Dean, Search Committee Chair, at gregg.dean@colostate.edu .  Questions about the application process may be directed to Lesley Jones at Lesley.J.Jones@colostate.edu .  About Fort Collins: Fort Collins is located along Colorado’s Front Range, approximately 65 miles north of Denver. The community combines access to outdoor recreation and a vibrant cultural environment with a strong innovation economy and proximity to regional, federal, and private-sector research partners. Additional information about living and working in the region, including community amenities and quality-of-life resources, is available on the Colorado State University Our Community page .  Additional Information: Learn more: Colorado State University | College of Veterinary Medicine and Biomedical Sciences | Department of Microbiology, Immunology, and Pathology Salary Range Already provided, just updating missing link on job requisition. Required Application Documents To apply, please upload the following applicant documents. Ensure your materials fully address the required and preferred job qualifications of the position. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Cover Letter, Resume/CV, Special Required Documentation Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    },
    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/School-of-Education-Instructor---Counseling-and-Career-Development---Open-Pool_R2026107658": {
      "title": "School of Education Instructor - Counseling and Career Development - Open Pool",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\n\nJob Description The School of Education seeks applications between September 22, 2026 - March 31, 2026, from individuals who are interested in securing temporary instructor positions within the Counseling and Career Development program for the 2026 – 2027 academic year. Instructors teach face-to-face graduate-level courses in areas of their expertise and are hired periodically for fall, spring, and/or summer term, contingent upon enrollments and need. Successful candidates may also be asked to provide clinical supervision and coordination of students’ practicum and/or internship experiences. Reappointment may depend upon performance and the availability of funding. Detailed descriptions of the School of Education and its faculty, programs, and courses are available on the web page at http://chhs.colostate.edu/soe/. Please contact program coordinator to discuss any instructional opportunities. Full Consideration Date: To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by 11:59 p.m. (MT) on March 31, 2027 . Compensation: $1,666.67 per credit hour instruction -- $50,000 base salary. Conditions of Employment: Pre-employment criminal background check (required for new hires). Required Job Qualifications: Earned master’s degree in counseling or closely-related degree. Licensed Professional Counselor in Colorado, Licensed  Professional Counselor Eligible in Colorado (and already licensed in another state), Colorado Special Services License – Professional School Counselor, Licensed Psychologist, or Licensed Clinical Social Worker. Evidence of excellence in teaching in the areas of Counseling and Career Development curriculum and/or clinical supervision. Preferred Job Qualifications: Earned doctorate degree in counselor education, preferably from a CACREP-accredited program. Experience teaching graduate students via face-to-face and distance technologies. Commitment to working with people from various backgrounds and inclusive teaching, scholarship and/or practice. Professional counselor educational background and identity. Application Instructions: Please upload a cover letter and CV/resume. This is an open pool posting. Applications will be reviewed as hiring needs arise, and qualified applicants may be contacted by individual faculty members if a suitable opportunity becomes available. This pool will expire on March 31, 2027 . Applicants wishing to be considered beyond this date must reapply. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    },
    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/Department-Head--Clinical-Sciences_R2026107650": {
      "title": "Department Head, Clinical Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nJob Description Colorado State University (CSU) is Colorado’s land-grant university and a Carnegie R1 research institution. CSU advances teaching, research, engagement, and service for the benefit of Colorado, the nation, and the world. Located in Fort Collins, Colorado, CSU offers a highly collaborative environment for interdisciplinary scholarship and education, with broad strengths in the life sciences, veterinary medicine, public health, agriculture, engineering, data science, and environmental sustainability. College of Veterinary Medicine and Biomedical Sciences: The CSU land grant mission, which permeates the college, is dedicated to education, research, service, and outreach.  CVMBS’ vision is to advance the well-being of animals, people, and the planet. CVMBS offers undergraduate, professional, and graduate courses of study, and confers Doctor of Veterinary Medicine, Master of Science and Doctor of Philosophy degrees in a range of biomedical and veterinary medical topic areas. The College is comprised of four departments: Biomedical Sciences; Clinical Sciences; Environmental Health and Radiological Sciences; and Microbiology, Immunology, and Pathology. CVMBS is fully accredited by the American Veterinary Medical Association, and has been highly ranked in national surveys, including U.S. News & World Report , Blue Ridge Institute , and Planetary Health Report Card . CVMBS faculty explore a variety of pivotal issues in human and animal health via world-renowned research programs in infectious disease, orthopedics, neuroscience, cancer biology, animal reproduction, and translational medicine, with annual extramural funding in the range of $60-100M. CVMBS has created the Veterinary Health System (VHS), which oversees management and operations of four clinical units and the state diagnostic laboratory to provide a collaborative and efficient approach to patient care delivered with the highest level of customer service, employee satisfaction, and advancements in medicine. Department of Clinical Sciences: The Department of Clinical Sciences has 115 tenure track and non-tenure track faculty who focus their efforts on the tripartite mission of teaching, research, and service. While approximately 75% of faculty provide some level of clinical services, growth and diversification of departmental goals have led to approximately 25% of faculty having a primary focus in research, education, or outreach. The department has 100 staff employees, 150 student or non-student hourly employees, and 100 house officers and graduate students. Clinical Sciences is one of CSU’s largest academic departments, supporting a complex portfolio that includes approximately $164M in annual activity across operations, research, teaching, philanthropy, and endowment-supported initiatives. The department plays a significant role in advancing the university’s academic, research, and clinical missions through the stewardship of diverse funding sources and programs. The Department of Clinical Sciences faculty and staff are dedicated to advanced medicine, excellent teaching, compassionate care, and discoveries benefiting the health of animals and people. It offers high-quality education programs for professional veterinary medical students, graduate veterinarians, and the public through the Small Animal Specialty Hospital, Johnson Family Equine Hospital, and Equine Reproductive Center. A new Livestock Hospital and Primary Care Clinic opened to the public in 2026.  These two new hospitals are part of the Phase 1 construction of the Veterinary Hospital and Education Center (VHEC), which provides state-of-the art educational facilities for all four veterinary classes in a Leadership in Energy and Environmental Design (LEED) and WELL Building certified facility.  VHEC opened for all students in Fall, 2026, and the new Ascend veterinary curriculum is being delivered to the incoming DVM class of 2030. Position Summary: CVMBS invites applications and nominations for the position of Department Head for Clinical Sciences in the College of Veterinary Medicine and Biomedical Sciences (CVMBS). This is an exciting opportunity for an individual to provide strategic, visionary leadership in one of the Nation's leading colleges of veterinary medicine. This is a 12-month leadership position with an expectation for a tenured full professor appointment in the Department of Clinical Sciences. Position targeted to start spring or summer of 2027.  The Department Head reports to the Dean of CVMBS and serves as a member of the College’s senior leadership team. The Department Head of Clinical Sciences will provide leadership and oversight for over 400 faculty, residents, interns and staff, and will be responsible for creating a focus and vision for the Department that meets current societal challenges and needs. The Department is administratively organized into sections that affiliate scholarly and clinical service efforts in the disciplines of anesthesiology, cardiology, critical care and emergency medicine, dermatology, epidemiology and preventive medicine, exotic animal medicine, equine medicine and surgery, food animal and livestock medicine and surgery, neurology, oncology, ophthalmology, small animal medicine and surgery, and theriogenology. The department head works closely with the VHS as a bridge for faculty with clinical duties. The current department organizational structure is described in the position prospectus .  Research programs in the Department of Clinical Sciences utilize state-of-the-art techniques to explore the pathogenesis of diseases affecting companion and production animals, and to develop new approaches for disease prevention and treatment. Major research interests include comparative oncology, orthopedics, cardiology, surgery, infectious disease, epidemiology, and neurology, and extend into human medical applications and discipline-based educational research. A full range of state-of-the-art imaging modalities, including digital radiography, fluoroscopy, positron emission tomography computed tomography, dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, nuclear medicine, diagnostic ultrasound, and magnetic resonance imaging with multinuclear spectroscopy capabilities are available within VHS. Faculty members in the Department are committed to teaching undergraduate, graduate, and professional veterinary medical students and have a strong reputation for innovation in instructional technology.   Full Consideration Date: October 30, 2026, 11:59pm (MT) Essential Duties:   Provide academic and scientific leadership in defining and attaining goals of the Department. Advance excellence and innovation in professional, graduate, and other educational programs. Promote excellence in all departmental endeavors, and develop a culture of belonging for all in the Department. Develop a departmental leadership structure that addresses departmental needs in a comprehensive and inclusive way.  Play a significant role in recruiting, hiring, and retaining faculty, and encourage mentorship for professional development and collegial interactions. Manage growth and development of the departmental missions in research, education, and service, including by leading departmental strategic planning to prioritize investment of time and resources.   Partner closely with leaders of the VHS and professional veterinary medical education programs to streamline and clarify faculty and staff appointments and budget. Develop innovative approaches for resourcing departmental operations and strategic plans. Serve as the primary departmental advocate in enhancing the visibility and prestige of the departmental sections and disciplines, at the Department, College, and University level  Represent the Department to external entities (professional and corporate organizations, alumni, etc.) and during fund-raising activities.  Manage fiscal planning and administration, direct and evaluate faculty and administrative staff, and facilitate relationships with industry and governmental entities that interact with the Department. Represent the department at the College Executive Committee. The Department Head may have the opportunity, with the agreement of the Dean, to be involved in additional teaching, clinical, and research activities, commensurate with the applicant’s professional and academic interests. Currently, the Department Head effort distribution includes an 80% administration component.  Perform Department Head responsibilities as outlined in the CSU Academic Faculty and Administrative Professional Manual.   Required Qualifications:   Advanced degree (e.g, DVM, BVSc, MVSc, MD, PhD, or equivalent). Demonstrated leadership experience in an academic, research, clinical, diagnostic, governmental, or similarly complex organization.  Commitment to, or potential for, enhancing veterinary medical education, graduate education, clinical service, and research. Academic or professional record qualified for appointment as a tenured full professor within the Department of Clinical Sciences. Evidence of successfully leading a large, diverse team. Outstanding communication skills. Commitment to, or potential for, enhancing community and belonging among all members of the department. Preferred Qualifications:  Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM) degree, board certification with veterinary specialty college, or equivalent. Demonstrated clinical veterinary experience. Experience in biomedical, translational, or clinical research.  Significant experience running an externally funded research program. Proven leadership ability and integrity, including developing a vision for the Department. Strong desire and proven track record to establish collaborative relationships within the College, University and with the private and public sectors. The ability to work productively and collegially with a large and diverse team.  Commitment to CVMBS values of Community, Integrity, Collaboration, and Innovation. Commitment to, or potential for, maintaining CSU's leadership in animal welfare and ethics  Effective planning and implementation of strategic initiatives. Conditions of Employment: Pre-employment criminal background check (required for new hires). Application Instructions: Applicants should submit the following through the CSU Jobs website Applications will not be considered complete until all listed documents have been submitted:  Cover letter describing experience relative to job responsibilities and applicant qualifications and attributes. A full Curriculum Vitae. A narrative of administrative and leadership philosophy. Applications will be treated confidentially. References will not be requested and contacted until finalists are chosen and consent is given for the search committee to collect references.  To ensure full consideration, applications must be submitted by October 30, 2026, 11:59pm (MT) and include all required application materials. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. General inquiries regarding the position can be directed to the Search Committee Chair, Sue James at susan.james@colostate.edu or (970) 231-1229. Inquiries, nominations, and applications will be kept confidential within the committee until finalists are named for campus interviews. References will not be contacted until the advanced stages of screening and candidates will receive prior notification.   Salary Range $250-300,000 Required Application Documents To apply, please upload the following applicant documents. Ensure your materials fully address the required and preferred job qualifications of the position. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Cover Letter, Resume/CV, Special Required Documentation Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    },
    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/Assistant-Professor_R2026107703": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nJob Description Position Summary: The Department of Occupational therapy is seeking one (1) nine-month, tenure track regular full-time faculty member at the rank of Assistant Professor to conduct and disseminate research; teach and mentor occupational therapy graduate (OTD & PhD) students and provide service to the Department, College and University. Brief Description of Academic Unit: The occupational therapy department seeks to optimize human performance and participation in everyday occupations, across all contexts and throughout the lifespan. We do this through excellence in teaching, research, service, and outreach. The Department includes a PhD in Occupation and Rehabilitation Science and an entry level OTD. Applicants are encouraged to visit the department website at https://www.chhs.colostate.edu/ot/ . Colorado State University (CSU) is a Carnegie Research I institution located in Fort Collins, 60 miles north of Denver, in a beautiful location along the Front Range of the Rocky Mountains. Enhanced by relationships with CSU, Fort Collins is a magnet for highly innovative new industries and is at the forefront of clean and alternative energy technologies, software/hardware sectors, telecommunications, aerospace and biotechnology. Northern Colorado’s strengths are recognized at the national level. For example, Fort Collins was included in the recent “Places of Invention” exhibit at the Smithsonian Institution’s National Museum of American History. Fort Collins also consistently ranks high in quality of life polls, and the Rocky Mountains provide world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. You will find award-winning schools, a thriving arts scene, a wide range of shops and restaurants, hundreds of miles of walking and biking paths, and a plethora of outdoor activities. Full Consideration Date: Sunday, November 1, 2026, 11:59pm (MT) Essential Duties: Teaching and Advising : (40%) Teach assigned courses; advise and mentor OTD and PhD students. Research : (40%) Conduct original research, write and submit grants, disseminate discovery through publication. The candidate is expected to develop a research program with both independent and collaborative efforts directed at advancing knowledge in the area of occupational therapy, rehabilitation science, occupational science, or other relevant field. ​Service : (20%) Provide service/outreach to the unit, college, university, and community in support of CSU’s mission. Serve on professional, institutional, and departmental committees to support research initiatives and the CSU land grant mission. Be a collaborative team member in the Department of Occupational Therapy. Supervision: May supervise future OTD and PhD or other CSU students. Conditions of Employment: Pre-employment Criminal Background Check (required for new hires). Work authorization visa sponsorship may be available depending on individual circumstances and associated costs for the selected finalist. Minimum Qualifications: Occupational therapy degree AND a terminal degree (PhD or equivalent) in a relevant discipline (occupational therapy, rehabilitation science, occupational science, or other relevant field). Demonstrated promise for extraordinary scholarship related to the study of human performance and participation in everyday occupations and contexts with evidence of research productivity or strong potential to establish a sustainable scholarly program (e.g., publications, presentation, grant activity). Commitment to building a focused program of research as evidenced by attempts to obtain intramural and/or extramural funding to support scholarship. Record of experience in, or demonstrated potential for, graduate-level teaching. Evidence of commitment to and collaboration with colleagues. Eligible for licensure as an occupational therapist in Colorado. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching/conducting qualitative or implementation research. Demonstrated experience in team science. Record of mentoring students in a research capacity. Record of teaching innovation. Applicant Instructions: For full consideration, submit the following application materials directly to the posting by application deadline: A cover letter indicating interest in the position at Colorado State University along with a description of the applicant’s ability to meet the position’s required and preferred qualifications; A Curriculum Vitae. Salary Range $75,000-$85,000 Required Application Documents To apply, please upload the following applicant documents. Ensure your materials fully address the required and preferred job qualifications of the position. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Cover Letter, Resume/CV Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    },
    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/LLC-Instructor----Open-Pool_R2026107860": {
      "title": "LLC Instructor -- Open Pool",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\n\nJob Description Position Summary: This is an open pool posting. When a position becomes available, the Department of Languages, Literatures & Cultures hires adjunct faculty from this applicant pool. Such faculty may be hired for the fall, spring, and/or summer term in a given academic year. They are hired to teach courses in language acquisition, linguistics, literature and culture in one or more of the following languages: American Sign Language, Arabic, Chinese, Hebrew, French, German, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Latin, Russian, and Spanish Applicants are added to the pool list throughout the calendar year. Hiring decisions are typically made during the late spring and early summer for fall semester, during the early fall semester for spring and during the spring semester for the summer term. Brief Work Unit Description: The Department of Languages, Literatures and Cultures is comprised of teachers and scholars of language, linguistics, literature and culture including specialists of second language acquisition, poetry, theater, cinema, and translation. Faculty represent over twenty different countries of origin. This work unit exists to educate, counsel, and support the undergraduate and graduate students in the department, maintain their records, and support the teaching, research and creative activity, and service of its faculty. Salary Range: $46,000 - $48,000 Essential Job Duties: Teaching (100%): Preparing lectures. Creating assignments. Holding office hours. Grading course materials. Conditions of Employment: Pre-employment criminal background check (required for new hires). Supervision: This position reports to the department chair. Minimum Qualifications: M.A. in a related field OR a combination of B.A. in a related field and one or more years of post-graduate professional experience in language pedagogy. Experience teaching a specific subject area and demonstrated teaching excellence. Advanced proficiency in the target language and proficiency in English. Experience teaching the language or literature. Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. Willingness to work together with LLC faculty as a team on curriculum building, assessment, student outreach and recruitment. Experience/expertise in curriculum development. Experience/expertise in assessment. Application Instructions: Applicants must meet the minimum qualifications in the announcement to be hired. For a complete application, please upload a cover letter, Curriculum Vitae, Statement of Teaching Philosophy, and a Statement of Teaching Interests. To document teaching excellence, applicants must also submit Course Materials and Sample Syllabus or Syllabi. Class or Student Evaluations are optional but encouraged. This is an open pool posting. Applications will be reviewed as hiring needs arise, and qualified applicants will be contacted if a suitable opportunity becomes available. This pool expires March 31, 2027. Individuals wishing to be considered beyond this date must reapply. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    },
    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/Assistant-Professor_R2026107707": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nJob Description Position Summary: The Department of Statistics at Colorado State University (CSU) invites applications for at least one Tenure-track Assistant Professor position. We welcome applicants working in a broad range of areas of Statistics. Candidates should have an established research program, a compelling plan for future research, the ability to supervise both graduate and undergraduate research, and an ability to achieve excellence in teaching. The salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, and includes a full benefits package. Work authorization visa sponsorship may be available based on the specific situation, including cost, for the selected final candidate. Department of Statistics: The department currently comprises 18 faculty and roughly 100 graduate students in our MS, MAS, and PhD graduate programs, and has a network of faculty affiliates at nearby research agencies (National Center for Atmospheric Research, National Institute of Standards and Technology, and Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, among others). Our faculty members have a wide range of expertise and are involved in various interdisciplinary graduate training and research activities. Internal and external consulting activities of the department are supported through the Graybill Statistics and Data Science Laboratory. Further information about the department and is available on our webpage http://statistics.colostate.edu/. Full Consideration Date: Applications completed by November 1, 2026 at 11:59 p.m. MST will receive full consideration, but applications may be accepted after this date until the position is ﬁlled. Essential Job Duties: Teach statistics courses at all levels. Advise MS and PhD students. Perform world class research in statistics. Write and publish papers, obtain grant funding. Perform service to the department. Serve on committees. Contribute to departmental initiatives such as curriculum development. Other related duties. Supervision: This position does not have any direct reports. Conditions of Employment: Pre-employment Criminal Background Check (required for all new hires). Minimum Qualifications: Terminal degree (Ph.D. or equivalent) in Statistics or a closely related field. Preferred Qualifications: Record of research accomplishments in statistics, data science, or probability. Ability to contribute in the areas of teaching and mentoring. An impactful future research agenda. Application Instructions: Please read the following instructions carefully and submit all required application materials.       To apply, please upload one single PDF containing all required application materials listed below, in the order provided. Your materials should clearly outline your work experience, education, and other relevant qualifications and demonstrate how your background aligns with the required and preferred qualifications outlined in the posting. The cover letter should describe your particular interest in CSU Statistics.   Cover Letter   Detailed CV   Research Statement   Teaching Statement     Important: The single PDF containing all application materials must be uploaded under the section labeled “Resume/CL.” Please combine all materials into one PDF and ensure they are included in the specified order. System limitations allow for a 5MB document upload. You will not be able to modify or add documents after submitting your application, so please carefully review your materials before submitting. Failure to submit the required materials as instructed may affect consideration of your application.     If you advance to the semifinalist stage, you will receive an email with instructions to provide the contact information for three professional references . To help avoid delays in the search process, please complete this step as soon as possible. Once you submit your references' contact information, each reference will receive an email with instructions for submitting a letter of recommendation. We will notify you with the deadline of when letters should be submitted at this stage in the hiring process.      Please note: For semi-finalist candidates, submitted letters of recommendation, along with application materials, will be made available to the faculty of the Department of Statistics for review.  Please direct questions about the application process to Ben Shaby at Ben.Shaby@colostate.edu . Salary Range $98,000 - $103,000 Required Application Documents To apply, please upload the following applicant documents. Ensure your materials fully address the required and preferred job qualifications of the position. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Cover Letter, Resume/CV, Statement of Teaching/Research Philosophy Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    },
    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/Adjunct-Faculty--Department-of-Accounting---Open-Pool_R2026107637": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Department of Accounting - Open Pool",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nPart time\n\nJob Description The Department of Accounting in the College of Business may hire temporary faculty from an applicant pool from time to time. The teaching load and course assignments are made by the Department Chair. Teaching could be days or evenings and live or online. Instructors may be hired for fall, spring and/or summer term in a given academic year. Applications will be accepted throughout the calendar year. Hiring decisions are normally made during the late spring and throughout the summer for fall semester, during fall semester for spring semester, and during spring semester for the summer term. Learn more about the Department of Accounting: https://biz.colostate.edu/resources/departments/department-of-accounting . Salary Range: Per course basis; default starting pay is $7,000 - $7,500/class; in select instances, pay may be higher commensurate with experience/course complexity. Essential Job Duties: Instructional Course Design and Administration: Construct course syllabus adhering to College of Business assurance of learning outcomes and departmental standards Administer course through Colorado State University’s learning management system. Instructional Course Delivery: Deliver instructional course material via multi-media teaching techniques in relevant subject areas in prescribed delivery format. Other duties as assigned. Supervision: N/A Conditions of Employment: Pre-employment Criminal Background Check (required for new hires). The successful candidate must be legally authorized to work in the United States by the proposed start date; the Department of Accounting will not sponsor a visa for this position now nor in the future. Minimum Qualifications Applicable Master’s, J.D., or Ph.D. that is aligned with one or more of the following subject areas: financial accounting, managerial accounting, tax, governmental accounting, auditing, accounting systems, and/or business ethics. Or current doctoral candidate in a field of study that is aligned with one or more of the above-mentioned subject areas. Or applicable undergraduate degree with five years or more professional work experience aligned with one or more of the above-mentioned subject areas. Ability to teach courses in one or more of the following areas: financial accounting, managerial accounting, tax, governmental accounting, auditing, accounting systems, and/or business ethics. Legal authorization to work in the US. The College of Business will not provide visa sponsorship for this position now or in the future. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching courses in these relevant areas: financial accounting, managerial accounting, tax, governmental accounting, auditing, accounting systems, and/or business ethics. Degree obtained from a school of business accredited by AACSB (Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business International). Previous university teaching experience in a college of business in relevant subject areas or experience teaching in a business setting. Substantial business experience in relevant subject areas. Experience with multi-media teaching techniques. Application Instructions: This is an open pool posting. Applications will be reviewed as hiring needs arise, and qualified applicants may be contacted if a suitable opportunity becomes available. This pool will expire on February 28, 2027 . Applicants wishing to be considered beyond this date must reapply. Applicants will be expected to provide: A cover letter indicating interest in the position at Colorado State University along with a description of the applicant’s ability to meet the position’s required and preferred qualifications. A resume/CV. Statement of Teaching Philosophy. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    },
    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/Adjunct-Faculty--Department-of-Computer-Information-Systems---Open-Pool_R2026107635": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Department of Computer Information Systems - Open Pool",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nPart time\n\nJob Description Position Summary: The Department of Computer Information Systems in the College of Business may hire temporary faculty from an applicant pool from time to time. The teaching load and course assignments are determined by the Department Chair. Instructors may be hired for fall, spring and/or summer term in a given academic year. Applications will be accepted throughout the calendar year. Hiring decisions are normally made during the late spring and throughout the summer for fall semester, during fall semester for spring semester, and during spring semester for the summer term. Learn more about the Department of Computer Information Systems: https://biz.colostate.edu/student-experience/departments/department-of-computer-information-systems . Salary Range: Per course basis; default starting pay is $7,000 - $7,500/class; in select instances, pay may be higher commensurate with experience/course complexity. Essential Job Duties: Instructional Course Design and Administration: Construct course syllabus adhering to College of Business assurance of learning outcomes and departmental standards. Administer course through Colorado State University’s learning management system. Instructional Course Delivery: Deliver instructional course material via multi-media teaching techniques in relevant subject areas in prescribed delivery format. Other duties as assigned. Supervision: N/A Conditions of Employment: Pre-employment Criminal Background Check (required for new hires). The successful candidate must be legally authorized to work in the United States by the proposed start date; the Department of Computer Information Systems will not sponsor a visa for this position now nor in the future. Minimum Qualifications: Applicable Master’s, J.D., or Ph.D. that is aligned with one or more of the following subject areas: AI, machine learning, analytics, cloud computing, computer programming, cybersecurity, data management, ERP, networking, project management, information systems, systems analysis and design, and web/mobile applications development. Or current doctoral candidate in a field of study that is aligned with one or more of the above-mentioned subject areas. Or applicable undergraduate degree with five years or more professional work experience aligned with one or more of the above-mentioned subject areas. Ability to teach courses in one or more of the following areas: AI, machine learning, analytics, cloud computing, computer programming, cybersecurity, data management, ERP, networking, project management, information systems, systems analysis and design, and web/mobile applications development. Legal authorization to work in the US. The College of Business will not provide visa sponsorship for this position now or in the future. Preferred Qualifications: Prior teaching experience in one or more of the following areas: AI, machine learning, analytics, cloud computing, computer programming, cybersecurity, data management, ERP, networking, project management, information systems, systems analysis and design, and web/mobile applications development. Degree obtained from a school of business accredited by AACSB (Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business International). Previous university teaching experience in a college of business in relevant subject areas or experience teaching in a business setting. Substantial business and information technology experience in relevant subject areas. Experience with multi-media teaching techniques. Application Instructions: This is an open pool posting. Applications will be reviewed as hiring needs arise, and qualified applicants may be contacted if a suitable opportunity becomes available. This pool will expire on February 28, 2027 . Applicants wishing to be considered beyond this date must reapply. Applicants will be expected to provide: A cover letter indicating interest in the position at Colorado State University along with a description of the applicant’s ability to meet the position’s required and preferred qualifications. A resume/CV. Statement of Teaching Philosophy. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    },
