    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/Department-Head--Design-and-Merchandising_R2026107606": {
      "title": "Department Head, Design and Merchandising",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nJob Description Position Summary: The Head of the Department of Design and Merchandising leads a dynamic team of faculty, staff, and students in pursuit of excellence in teaching, research, and engagement. Candidates are expected to have a record of scholarly excellence, academic leadership, and strategic vision consistent with leadership at an R1 land-grant University. You can learn more about the Department of Design and Merchandising here: https://www.chhs.colostate.edu/dm/ . Full Consideration Date: To receive full consideration, complete applications must be submitted by 11:59 p.m. Mountain Time on November 8, 2026. Applications received after this date and before the posting closes may be considered but are not guaranteed review. The posting will close at 11:59 p.m. Mountain Time on November 29, 2026. Essential Job Duties: The Director role is 75% administrative and 25% research & engagement.  Administrative responsibilities include: Leadership within and on behalf of the department. Strategic planning. Personnel management. Fiscal management. Facility oversight. Partnership on development/philanthropy and industry engagement efforts in support of the Department mission. Supporting the growth of the Department’s extramurally funded research portfolio. Service on the College of Health and Human Sciences cabinet.   The research and engagement activities include extramurally funded collaborative or independent research, community engagement, and both graduate student and faculty mentoring.    Supervision: The Director supervises all faculty and staff in the Department of Design and Merchandising (~30 FTE). Conditions of Employment: Pre-employment criminal background check required (for all new hires). Minimum Qualifications: Earned doctorate in apparel merchandising, interior architecture, textile sciences or related field. Academic credentials consistent with a faculty appointment at the rank of Professor with tenure at an R1 University. Demonstrated record of a strong research record characterized by national/international recognition. Demonstrated record of strategic and innovative leadership in leading teaching, research, and engagement efforts. Experience with fiscal management at the department/school level or higher. Experience with development/philanthropy and industry engagement. Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of university or national leadership in education such as: Professional journal editor or editorial board. Professional Society leadership. Service on or leadership for national grant review panels (federal or foundation sponsors). Evidence of leadership in innovative curriculum development. Evidence of innovation in faculty and staff professional development. Evidence of excellence in mentoring graduate students. Application Instructions: To apply, please upload all the following required application material in the Resume/Cover Letter section of the application: Cover Letter and Resume/CV (combined single PDF file preferred) Philosophy of Leadership (2 pages max) Research Statement (2 pages max) Ensure your materials fully address the required and preferred job qualifications of the position. Salary Range $215,000 - $225,000 Required Application Documents To apply, please upload the following applicant documents. Ensure your materials fully address the required and preferred job qualifications of the position. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Cover Letter, Resume/CV, Special Required Documentation, Statement of Teaching/Research Philosophy Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    },
    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/Instructional-Coordinator---Adjunct---Open-Pool_R2026107633": {
      "title": "Instructional Coordinator - Adjunct - Open Pool",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nPart time\n\nJob Description Position Summary: Instructional Coordinators (ICs) bring professional-level industry experience in the specific content areas of the MBA and/or MCIS programs. This experience adds value and reinforces academic content to the students enrolled in the College’s online graduate programs. Instructional Coordinators provide a high level of student outreach and have the availability to frequently connect with students, academic advisors and team leads. They must be engaging, offering an increased and innovative presence in the online classroom to best serve the student and facilitate student success. Instructional Coordinators are expected to provide substantial and specific student feedback and offer a quick turnaround on grades. Instructional Coordinators reflect department and institutional values, and they are expected to foster the college’s commitment to CSU’s mission. Instructional Coordinators may be hired for fall, spring and/or summer term in a given academic year. Applications will be accepted throughout the calendar year. Hiring decisions are normally made during the late spring and throughout the summer for fall semester, during fall semester for spring semester, and during spring semester for the summer term. Visit https://biz.colostate.edu/student-experience/departments to learn more. Salary Range: Per student basis, commensurate with grading intensity/course size, $70 – $275/student + potential pay lead instructor duties $500 - $1,600/course depending on credits. Essential Job Duties: Instructional Coordination: Reinforce, re-teach, and tutor concepts to students in online sections. This includes teaching the application of concepts from theory in the classroom to practice in industry/career environment based on professional experience in various concept areas. Grade all student assignments, submissions, and discussions to assess mastery of course content. Hold virtual office hours (by phone, Web conference, or chat) to provide additional reinforcement of course concepts or tutoring students who need additional reinforcement. Student Communication: Instructional Coordinators oversee course sections of 30-40 online students per section, serving as primary liaison between course content and communication for online students via email, phone, or web conference. Course Preparation: Review course materials and lectures in preparation for serving the students.  Other duties as assigned. Supervision: None Conditions of Employment: Pre-employment criminal background check (required for new hires) Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States by proposed start date. The College of Business will not sponsor a visa for these positions. Minimum Qualifications: For those applying for the IC - MBA: MBA, MSBA degree or equivalent from a school of business accredited by the AACSB—(The Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business International), OR earned Master’s, JD degree, OR PhD. or PhD. candidate in a relevant field of study, or DBA or equivalent. Five years of full-time professional experience with a demonstrated progression in responsibility and authority, or equivalent teaching experience in required topic area. Excellent written communication skills. Demonstrated ability to self-direct and self-motivate. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint). Experience delivering supplemental teaching/coaching to students in order to promote mastery of course content and to provide specific feedback to foster understanding of content. Willingness and ability to work weekends, early morning hours, and evening hours.* Applicants must have technical and academic current skills/experience in one or more of the following content areas to serve in the MBA program as an Instructional Coordinator: Accounting, Marketing, Leadership, International Business, Finance, Economics, Legal and Ethical Business Environment, Strategy, Human Resources, Supply Chain, and Statistics. Applicants must have the technology required to work online, the ability to load necessary software required to serve the students, or have access to this technology. Legal authorization to work in the US. For those applying for the IC - MCIS: MBA, MSBA, MCIS degree or equivalent from a school of business accredited by the AACSB—(The Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business International), OR earned Master’s, JD degree, OR PhD. or PhD. candidate in a relevant field of study. Excellent written communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint). Experience delivering supplemental teaching/coaching to students in order to promote mastery of course content and to provide specific feedback to foster understanding of content. Applicants must have current technical and academic skills/experience in one or more of the following content areas to serve as Instructional Coordinator in the MCIS program: IT infrastructure and management, ERP, network administration, Linux and Windows use and administration, programming/scripting (e.g., C#, ASP.Net, PHP, Java, bash, PowerShell, Python, R, JavaScript, HTML, CSS), database concepts and design, UML & ER diagramming and modeling, SQL, NoSQL, systems analysis and design, cybersecurity, project management, analytics, machine learning, visualization, and business intelligence. Applicants must have the technology required to serve students online, including the ability to load the necessary software to facilitate course material, or have access to this technology. Legal authorization to work in the US. Preferred Qualifications: 2+ Years’ experience in the online learning environment. 2+ Years’ experience using a Learning Management System (LMS) such as Canvas (Instructure), Blackboard, Moodle, etc. Demonstrated experience in AdWords, WordPress, SEO, or other marketing data analytical tools. Application Instructions: This is an open pool posting. Applications will be reviewed as hiring needs arise, and qualified applicants may be contacted if a suitable opportunity becomes available. This pool will expire on February 28, 2027 . Applicants wishing to be considered beyond this date must reapply. Applicants will be expected to provide: A cover letter indicating interest in the position at Colorado State University along with a description of the applicant’s ability to meet the position’s required and preferred qualifications. A resume/CV. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    },
    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/Assistant-Professor_R2026107783": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nJob Description Position Summary: The Department of Chemistry at Colorado State University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Experimental Physical Chemistry at the Assistant Professor level. Applicants whose research complements and strengthens research themes in the Department of Chemistry and across the Colorado State University research enterprise are especially encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will be expected to contribute to chemistry education excellence in the Department, including teaching physical chemistry courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The Department of Chemistry at Colorado State University comprises approximately 30 tenure-track and tenured faculty and more than 180 graduate students, with research spanning analytical, biological, inorganic, materials, organic, and physical chemistry. Faculty and students participate in interdisciplinary research across the University, and the Department has a strong tradition of undergraduate participation in research. Research is supported by the Analytical Resources Core, which provides extensive shared instrumentation and 24/7 access for trained users. Further information about the department and is available on our webpage http://chem.colostate.edu Work authorization visa sponsorship may be available based on the specific situation, including cost, for the selected final candidate. Full Consideration Date: Applications completed by November 1, 2026 at 11:59 p.m. MST will receive full consideration, but applications may be accepted after this date until the position is ﬁlled. Essential Job Duties:  Develop and maintain an independent, externally funded research program in experimental physical chemistry. Disseminate research findings through peer-reviewed publications and presentations. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in chemistry. Mentor and advise undergraduate and graduate students in research. Participate in departmental, college, and university service and contribute to the academic mission of the Department. Perform other duties as assigned. Supervision:  This position does not have any direct reports. Conditions of Employment:  Pre-employment Criminal Background Check (required for all new hires). Minimum Qualifications:  Ph.D. in Chemistry or a closely related field. Evidence of research productivity or strong potential to establish a sustainable scholarly program (e.g., publications, presentations, grant activity). Demonstrated ability to teach effectively at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Preferred Qualifications: Record of research accomplishments in experimental physical chemistry. Postdoctoral research experience or equivalent professional research experience. Ability to contribute in the areas of teaching and mentoring. Potential to establish an impactful, externally funded research program. Application Instructions: Please read the following instructions carefully and submit all required application materials.       To apply, please upload one single PDF containing all required application materials listed below, in the order provided. Your materials should clearly outline your work experience, education, and other relevant qualifications and demonstrate how your background aligns with the required and preferred qualifications outlined in the posting. The cover letter should describe your particular interest in CSU Chemistry.    Cover Letter  Detailed CV  Research Statement  Teaching Statement    Important: The single PDF containing all application materials must be uploaded under the section labeled “Resume/CL.” Please combine all materials into one PDF and ensure they are included in the specified order. System limitations allow for a 5MB document upload. You will not be able to modify or add documents after submitting your application, so please carefully review your materials before submitting. Failure to submit the required materials as instructed may affect consideration of your application.     If you advance to the semifinalist stage, you will receive an email with instructions to provide the contact information for three professional references . To help avoid delays in the search process, please complete this step as soon as possible. Once you submit your references' contact information, each reference will receive an email with instructions for submitting a letter of recommendation. We will notify you with the deadline of when letters should be submitted at this stage in the hiring process.      Please note: For semi-finalist candidates, submitted letters of recommendation, along with application materials, will be made available to the faculty of the Department of Chemistry for review.  Please direct questions about the application process to Jean Chung at jean.chung@colostate.edu . Salary Range $93-000- $95,000 Required Application Documents To apply, please upload the following applicant documents. Ensure your materials fully address the required and preferred job qualifications of the position. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Cover Letter, Resume/CV, Statement of Teaching/Research Philosophy Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    },
    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/Assistant-Professor---Department-of-Physics_R2026108037": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Department of Physics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nJob Description Position Summary: The Department of Physics at Colorado State University (CSU) invites applications for a Tenure-track Assistant Professor position. We welcome applicants working in theoretical and computational condensed Physics. The appointed individual is expected to actively participate in the teaching/mentoring/advising of undergraduate students, graduate students, post-doctoral scholars, including classroom teaching. They are also expected to build and operate a forward-looking and internationally recognized research program. Participation in department and university service and administrative governance, engagement in scholarly/professional endeavors, and fulfilling general faculty responsibilities is expected. These activities are vital to the teaching, research, and service missions of Colorado State University.  For full consideration, applications and materials must be submitted by 11:59 p.m. MST, December 3, 2026. This position will remain open until filled. Work authorization visa sponsorship may be available based on the specific situation, including cost, for the selected final candidate. Work Unit Description: The Department of Physics is an academic department within the College of Natural Sciences. It has 21 faculty members with research programs primarily in the areas of atomic, molecular, and optical physics; high-energy and particle astrophysics, and condensed matter physics. Essential Job Duties:  Teach and mentor students at the undergraduate and graduate levels, including course and curriculum development. Conduct and publish research, pursue external funding, and contribute to scholarly advancement in the field. Provide service to the department, university, profession, and community in support of CSU’s mission. Other duties as assigned. Conditions of Employment: Pre-employment background check (required for all new hires). Supervision: Graduate Research Assistants. Undergraduate Research Assistants. FTE will vary and will be commensurate with the scope of the research program. Minimum Qualifications:  PhD or equivalent terminal degree in Physics of a related field. Evidence of research productivity and potential to establish a sustainable scholarly program in the research area of theoretical and computational theoretical physics (e.g., publications, presentations, grant activity). Evidence of ability to teach effectively at the undergraduate and/or graduate level.  Preferred Qualifications: A strong record demonstrating potential to contribute to teaching/mentoring/advising of undergraduate and graduate students.  A strong record of scholarly/professional preparation and record of past research accomplishments. A proposed research plan that is innovative, aligns with the interests of the Department and College, is of quality and has a high likelihood of success, can lead to an internationally recognized research program with external funding.   Potential to contribute to service for the university, the profession of physics, and the public. Application Instructions: Please read the following instructions carefully and submit all required application materials.       To apply, please upload one single PDF containing all required application materials listed below, in the order provided. Your materials should clearly outline your work experience, education, and other relevant qualifications and demonstrate how your background aligns with the required and preferred qualifications outlined in the posting. Cover Letter that addresses specific interests in CSU and its Department of Physics; A complete curriculum vitae; A teaching statement, limited to 3 pages; A research statement, limited to 4 pages (references do not count towards the page limit).   Important: System limitations allow for a 5MB document upload. You will not be able to modify or add documents after submitting your application, so please carefully review your materials before submitting. Failure to submit the required materials as instructed may affect consideration of your application.     If you advance to the semifinalist stage, you will receive an email with instructions to provide the contact information for three professional references . To help avoid delays in the search process, please complete this step as soon as possible.   Once you submit your references' contact information, each reference will receive an email with instructions for submitting a letter of recommendation. We will notify you with the deadline of when letters should be submitted at this stage in the hiring process.        Please note: For semi-finalist candidates, submitted letters of recommendation, along with application materials, will be made available to the faculty of the Department of Physics for review.    Please direct questions about the application process to Jacob Roberts at Jacob.Roberts@colostate.edu . Salary Range $91,000 - $95,000 Required Application Documents To apply, please upload the following applicant documents. Ensure your materials fully address the required and preferred job qualifications of the position. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Cover Letter, Resume/CV, Statement of Teaching/Research Philosophy Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    },
    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-in-Equine-Surgery---Education_R2026107943": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor in Equine Surgery & Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nJob Description Position Summary: The Department of Clinical Sciences (DCS) at Colorado State University invites applications for a 12-month Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Equine Surgery and Surgical Education. The successful candidate will share clinical responsibilities at the Johnson Family Equine Hospital (JFEH) with 3 tenure track surgeons and a broad-based team of experienced veterinary technicians. Currently there are 3 Equine Surgery and Lameness residents. The candidate will be primarily responsible for clinical service with a commitment of 18 - 24 weeks on duty pending other research and teaching commitments. There are no primary duty after hours requirements of the position. However, the position will back up Equine Critical Care Surgeons for orthopedic emergencies. The candidate will be expected to participate in the teaching of professional veterinary medical and graduate students, and it is anticipated they will provide continuing education to veterinarians and veterinary technicians. As CSU begins a new curriculum in the fall of 2026, this hire will be expected to participate in the surgical skills training of students starting in their first year of the curriculum. The training will occur in the “VetReady” stream of the Ascend (new) curriculum. Additional didactic contributions and participation in educational blocks are also anticipated. Finally, the successful candidate will participate in surgical skills training for second year students and Fundamentals of Surgery for Third year of the legacy curriculum as it is phased out over the next one to two years.   The DCS, and JFEH are located on the South Campus of Colorado State University and have maintained a strong tradition of excellence in Equine Surgery and Lameness with successful DVM (all 4 years) and post-graduate (house officer) training programs. In addition to hospital services and educational opportunities provided at the JFEH, growth in teaching programs is anticipated with the opening of a new building dedicated to DVM education and primary care in August 2026.   The south campus facilities maintain state-of-the-art equipment with plans to enhance these within the small animal specialty hospital over the next few years. The state-of-the-art Equine Hospital (JFEH) opened in September 2021, and the new Livestock hospital opened in June 2026. The JFEH includes new surgical facilities, a dedicated lameness facility with hard and soft surfaces, CT  (to enable standing and recumbent procedures), digital radiology and ultrasound. The Translational Medicine Institute (Adjacent to the JFEH) houses an additional CT for anesthetized cases and a 3T MRI for anesthetized cases. The JFEH houses equine specialties in surgery, internal medicine, sports medicine, anesthesia, dentistry, ophthalmology, diagnostic imaging, and critical care and shares specialists in cardiology, dermatology, reproduction and others with the larger Veterinary Health System. The JFEH also has a vibrant primary care Equine Field and Podiatry Service. In addition to providing veterinary services to local clients CSU is a preeminent tertiary care facility with a broad-based caseload to support numerous primary (e.g., internal medicine, ophthalmology, oncology) and support (e.g., anesthesia, imaging, pathology) services.   In addition to investigator driven research, collaborative opportunities exist for partnership with clinical and basic science departments within the college, university colleagues, as well as with nearby institutions including Poudre Valley Hospital, the University of Colorado, Denver Children’s Hospital, and regional biomedical facilities. The state-of-the-art research facility (C. Wayne McIlwraith Translational Medicine Institute) adjacent to the JFEH offers additional opportunities for translational medical research and veterinary medical continuing education. For full consideration, applications must be submitted through Workday by 11:59pm (MT) on Monday, November 16, 2026. Email or mail-in applications will not be accepted. This position will be open until filled. Work authorization visa sponsorship may be available based on the specific situation for the selected final candidate. A signing bonus may be considered for successful candidates. Essential Job Duties:  Teaching : Clinical – Provide 18-24 weeks of clinical effort per year to include active instruction to 3rd and 4th year Veterinary Medical students and participation in the clinical training of visitors, interns and residents rotating through the Equine Surgery and Lameness service. Participation in shared backup after-hours coverage when on clinical duty is anticipated for orthopedic emergencies. Promoting minimally invasive surgery training, including training house officers in minimally invasive surgery is desired. Didactic – The candidate will provide didactic teaching within the Clinical Sciences graduate program and the DVM Professional curriculum. The candidate will also be expected to actively participate in journal club and other resident training opportunities. Candidates are also invited to participate in the ongoing DVM curriculum renewal process or ASCEND curriculum. Laboratory – The candidate will provide laboratory training in the Surgical Skills portion of the ASCEND VetReady stream (new curriculum), Second Year Foundations Surgical Skills, and the Fundamentals of Surgery Laboratory in third year. They will also participate in the Third Year Large Animal Procedures Laboratory and the Equine Advanced Procedures Laboratory. Experience and skills associated with minimally invasive surgery in the teaching of veterinary students would be beneficial. Research: The candidate is expected to develop a research program with both independent and collaborative efforts directed at advancing knowledge in the area of equine surgery and/or surgical education. Training house officers in developing research skills toward publication as required by the ACVS is an expectation. Service/Outreach: Clinical Assignment – Provide 18-24 weeks of clinical effort to the JFEH per year. Participation in shared backup after-hours coverage for orthopedic emergencies when on clinical duty is anticipated. In addition to being able to manage all varieties of surgical cases, a strong interest in upper respiratory, laparoscopy/thoracoscopy and soft tissue surgery is desired to enable the advancement of soft tissue surgery cases in the JFEH. Conditions of Employment: Pre-employment Criminal Background Check (required for new hires). Minimum Qualifications:  DVM or equivalent veterinary professional degree. Board Certification in the American College of Veterinary Surgeons (ACVS) or equivalent. Surgical skills education training experience. Preferred Qualifications: Advanced degree or research focused post-doctoral fellowship. Experience instructing veterinary students, interns, and residents in the practice of equine surgery and lameness. Minimally Invasive Surgery Fellowship Training. Expertise and clinical interests in soft tissue surgery, particularly in upper respiratory and minimally invasive abdominal/thoracic surgery. Salary Range Assistant Professor $148,000 – $160,000 Associate Professor $170,000 – $182,000 Required Application Documents To apply, please upload the following applicant documents. Ensure your materials fully address the required and preferred job qualifications of the position. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Cover Letter, Resume/CV Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    },
    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/Assistant-Professor_R2026107939-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nJob Description Position Summary: The Department of Food Science and Human Nutrition (FSHN) is seeking applications for Assistant Professors in the area of Nutrition Science. The 9-month tenure/tenure track appointment will begin August 16, 2027. The Assistant Professor will develop and maintain a nationally recognized, externally funded research program in nutrition science that complements departmental research in areas such as cardiometabolic health, nutrient metabolism, functional foods, vascular function, and nutritional immunology. This position integrates research with existing department, college, and university priorities; teaches and mentors undergraduate and graduate students; and contributes to collaborative research activities with academic and industry partners. Successful candidates are expected to establish a nationally recognized, externally funded research program, integrate their research into existing department, college, and university priority areas, and teach and mentor undergraduate and graduate students. The position will have outstanding department support, strong research infrastructure, and access to collaborative opportunities both within CSU and with academic industry partners. Faculty in the Department of Food Science and Human Nutrition conduct innovative research in state of the art facilities, with an emphasis on basic, translational, and clinical applications in chronic lifestyle-related diseases. To learn more, please visit https://www.chhs.colostate.edu/fshn/ Full Consideration Date: please apply by Monday, 11/09/2026, 11:59pm (MT). Essential Job Duties: Research/Scholarly Activity Teaching/Advising/Mentoring Service/Outreach/Engagement Conditions of Employment: Pre-employment Background Check (required for all new hires). Supervision: Undergraduate and Graduate student researchers. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Nutrition or any related field. At least 2 years of postdoctoral experience or previous academic appointment. Demonstrated record of peer-reviewed research publications in high-impact journals. Demonstrated ability to acquire research funding. Demonstrated ability to teach and mentor undergraduate and/or graduate students. Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of interdisciplinary research and successful team-based collaboration. Experience writing and obtaining large external grants. Salary Range $75,000-$85,000 Required Application Documents To apply, please upload the following applicant documents. Ensure your materials fully address the required and preferred job qualifications of the position. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Cover Letter, Resume/CV, Statement of Teaching/Research Philosophy Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    },
    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/Assistant-Professor_R2026108140": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nJob Description Position Summary: The Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology invites applications to fill a tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor level. Applications will be considered from individuals with research interests and backgrounds in the broadly defined areas of biomolecular interactions, assembly and regulation of macromolecular complexes, mechanistic biochemistry, and/or structural biology. The Department has outstanding research programs in the areas of molecular biology, cellular biochemistry, and macromolecular structure & function, and this position is part of the department’s initiative to further broaden expertise in biophysics, biochemistry, structural biology, and/or chemical biology. The successful candidate is expected to develop or maintain an internationally recognized externally funded research program that complements current departmental strengths, participate in undergraduate and graduate education, and provide service through Departmental, College, and University committees, as well as contributions to the profession. The position requires a firm commitment to undergraduate and graduate education and reflects departmental and university values as a land grant institution. Description of Work Unit: The Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology (BMB) is one of eight departments in the College of Natural Sciences at Colorado State University. The Department is home to over 280 undergraduate majors, 40 graduate students, 30 postdoctoral fellows and research associates, and 19 tenure-stream faculty members. The regular faculty currently generates over $10M per year in total research funding. The faculty is further strengthened by a group of instructional faculty, research faculty, and joint faculty appointments from the Departments of Biomedical Sciences and of Chemical & Biological Engineering. Many BMB faculty members participate in one or more of the interdisciplinary graduate programs [Cell and Molecular Biology / Molecular, Cellular and Integrative Neuroscience / Biomedical Engineering]. The Department is primarily housed in the Molecular and Radiological Biosciences Building, which it shares with the Department of Environmental and Radiological Health Sciences, with additional renovated space in the Anatomy/Zoology Building. As a land-grant institution, Colorado State University (CSU) offers a broad range of instructional programs in the biological, biomedical, veterinary, and agricultural sciences. On campus enrollment totals over 30,000 students. More information about Colorado State University can be obtained https://visit.colostate.edu/plan-your-visit/. Work authorization visa sponsorship may be available based on the specific situation, including cost, for the selected final candidate. Full Consideration Date: November 16, 2026; 11:59 (MST). Essential Job Duties: Teach and mentor students at the undergraduate and graduate levels, including course and curriculum development. Conduct and publish research, acquire external funding to support research, and contribute to scholarly advancement in the field. Provide service to the department, university, profession, and community in support of CSU’s mission. Other duties as assigned. Conditions of Employment: Pre-employment background check (required for all new hires). Supervision: This position does not have any direct reports. Minimum Qualifications: Terminal degree (Ph.D. or equivalent) in the relative discipline. Postdoctoral research training. Evidence of research productivity and/or strong potential to establish a sustainable scholarly research program through publications, presentations, and/or grant activities. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated ability to teach effectively at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Demonstrated ability to obtain funding through fellowships, grants or other types of external support. Research program that addresses mechanistic questions in biological systems at the level of molecular structure, interactions, and/or dynamics. A strong commitment to collegiality and collaborative research. Application Instructions: Please read the following instructions carefully and submit all required application materials. To apply, please upload a single PDF containing all required application materials listed below, in the order provided. Your materials should clearly outline your work experience, education, and other relevant qualifications and demonstrate how your background aligns with the required and preferred qualifications outlined in the posting. The required application materials include: A cover letter that addresses specific interests in CSU and its Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology (limited to 2 pages); A complete curriculum vitae; A teaching statement (limited to 2 pages); A research statement (limited to 3 pages); Optional: One (maximum) reprint of a representative publication. After submitting your application, you will receive an email with instructions to provide the contact information for three professional references. To help avoid delays in the search process, please complete this step as soon as possible. Once your references’ contact information has been received, each reference will receive an email with instructions for submitting a letter of recommendation. Letters of recommendation must be received by November 30, 2026. Please note: For semi-finalist candidates, submitted letters of recommendation, along with application materials, will be made available to the faculty of the Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology for review.  Please direct questions about the application process to Nina Lambert, at nina.lambert@colostate.edu . Salary Range $87,000 to $89,000 Salary is commensurate with experience and qualifications. A start-up package appropriate for the research area will be made available. Required Application Documents To apply, please upload the following applicant documents. Ensure your materials fully address the required and preferred job qualifications of the position. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Cover Letter, Resume/CV, Statement of Teaching/Research Philosophy Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    },
    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/Adjunct-Instructor--ESS-SOCR-405-Global-Agriculture-and-Environmental-Change_R2026107957": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor: ESS/SOCR 405 Global Agriculture and Environmental Change",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nJob Description Position Summary: The Department of Soil and Crop Sciences is seeking an instructor to teach ESS/SOCR 405: Global Agriculture and Environmental Change Spring semester 2027 as well as the online classes. This class will explore the past, present, and future of global agroecosystems in a changing environment. We will examine a range of environmental issues facing agroecosystems around the world, including water management, climate change, air pollution, and land use change. We will also assess the history of agricultural development and the factors that determine food security, as well as what strategies could help create a more sustainable and food secure world. The instructor will demonstrate effective communication skills. S/He will provide teaching excellence of the subject matter and strive for improvement of the undergraduate experience. Full Consideration Date: please apply by Monday, November 9, 2026, 11:59pm (MT). Work Unit Description: The Department of Soil and Crop Sciences is focused on education, research, and outreach to solve the world’s most pressing food production issues and crucial matters about Earth, its ecosystems, and their services. Our faculty and staff apply research-based solutions to benefit Colorado and the world. We offer academic programs to prepare students to address national and global crop production, sustainability, and environmental quality challenges such as waste management, water quality, and reclamation of drastically disturbed lands. There are numerous opportunities for students to be involved in cutting edge research related to global food production and ecosystem function and protection. Essential Job Duties: Present class lectures for ESS/SOCR 405, both in person and online for spring 2027; respond to student questions; course material preparation; student evaluation/grading exams. Conditions of Employment: Pre-employment criminal background check (required for new hires). Authorized to work in the United States by employment start date.   Supervision: This position will not supervise any employees. Minimum Qualifications: PhD in Natural Resources or a closely related field . At least 3 years of postdoctoral experience in global food systems research. At least 3 years of experience teaching asynchronous courses. Demonstrated ability to teach hybrid courses in areas of expertise using video conferencing, synchronous, and/or asynchronous learning technologies. Payment for teaching online 801 sections will follow Soil and Crop Sciences' policy. Salary Range $7,500/semester for teaching a 3 credit course Required Application Documents To apply, please upload the following applicant documents. Ensure your materials fully address the required and preferred job qualifications of the position. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Cover Letter, Resume/CV Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    },
    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/Assistant-Professor--Genotypes-to-Phenotypes_R2026108071": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor: Genotypes to Phenotypes",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nJob Description Position Summary: The Department of Biology at Colorado State University invites applications for at least one tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level. We seek creative, collaborative biologists working in any multicellular eukaryotic system (model species and/or natural populations) whose research investigates how genetic variation gives rise to phenotypes in areas such as functional genomics, evolutionary genomics, quantitative and statistical genetics, and computational and systems biology.  We welcome experimental, computational, and statistical genetic approaches, from genome-wide association tests, genome editing, functional screens, and single-cell and multi-omic profiling to machine learning and sequence-based language models. We are particularly interested in candidates whose research elucidates the effects of complex genotype-environment interactions on phenotypic variation that affects organismal function, fitness, and interactions with the environment. Work authorization visa sponsorship may be available based on the specific situation, including cost, for the selected final candidate. Applications completed by November 15, 2026, at 11:59 p.m. MST, will receive full consideration, but applications may be accepted after this date until the position is ﬁlled. Department Information: The Department of Biology at Colorado State University is a collaborative community dedicated to research, teaching, mentoring, and outreach across the full breadth of biology, from molecular and cellular biology to ecology and evolution. As a hub for the life sciences at CSU, the department connects faculty and students with interdisciplinary programs in cell and molecular biology, neuroscience, ecology, sustainability, and biomedical engineering. Further information about the department is available on our webpage: https://www.biology.colostate.edu/ Essential Job Duties:  Disseminate research findings through publication in peer-reviewed journals and presentations at national and international conferences. Establish and sustain an independent, externally funded research program. Teach and develop undergraduate and graduate courses. Mentor and advise trainees. Service to the department and university, such as serving on committees and overseeing curriculum development. Minimum Qualifications:  Ph.D. in biology or a related field, such as genetics, biochemistry, organismal biology, evolutionary biology, or biomedical sciences. At least one year of postdoctoral experience by the start of the position. Record of publications in genotype-to-phenotype research. Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of writing successful grants or fellowships. Experience teaching and mentoring graduate and undergraduate students. Conditions of Employment: Pre-employment Background Check (required for new hires). Application Instructions: Please read the following instructions carefully and submit all required application materials.  To apply, please upload one single PDF containing all required application materials listed below, in the order provided. A cover letter describing your qualification and interest in the position. A detailed CV. A 2-3-page research statement. A 1-page teaching statement. Important: System limitations allow for a 5MB  document upload. You will not be able to modify or add documents after submitting your application, so please carefully review your materials before submitting. Failure to submit the required materials as instructed may affect consideration of your application. If you advance to the semifinalist stage, you will receive an email with instructions to provide contact information for three professional references . To help avoid delays in the search process, please complete this step as soon as possible. Once you submit your references' contact information, each reference will receive an email with instructions for submitting a letter of recommendation. We will notify you with the deadline for when letters should be submitted at this stage in the hiring process.   Please direct questions about the application process to Chris Funk at Chris.Funk@colostate.edu Please note: For semi-finalist candidates, submitted letters of recommendation, along with application materials, will be made available to the faculty of the Department of Biology for review.  Salary Range $83,000-$97,000 Required Application Documents To apply, please upload the following applicant documents. Ensure your materials fully address the required and preferred job qualifications of the position. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Cover Letter, Resume/CV, Statement of Teaching/Research Philosophy Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    },
    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/Anthropology-and-Geography-Instructors---Open-Pool_R2026108260": {
      "title": "Anthropology and Geography Instructors - Open Pool",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nPart time\n\nJob Description Position Summary: Instructors are hired (as needed) for a single semester to teach introductory (and occasionally upper-division) in-person courses in archaeology, cultural and biological anthropology, or geography. As positions become available, the chair will reach out to applicants directly. Work Unit Description: Home - Anthropology and Geography | Colorado State University Salary Range: $46,000 - $48,000 Essential Job Duties: Essential job duties vary depending on the course, but may include: Preparing lectures Creating assignments Holding office hours Grading course materials Specific duties will be defined at the time of hire by the supervisor. Supervision: This position reports to the Department Chair of Sociology. Conditions of Employment: Pre-employment criminal background check (required for all new hires). Minimum Qualifications: A Master’s degree in anthropology, geography or related field is required. Prior experience teaching at the university level. Preferred Qualifications: A Ph.D. is preferred. Application Instructions: To apply, please upload a CV and cover letter. This is an evergreen posting. Applications will be reviewed as hiring needs arise, and qualified applicants may be contacted by individual faculty members if a suitable opportunity becomes available. This pool will expire on March 31, 2027 . Applicants wishing to be considered beyond this date must reapply. Search Contact: Please contact Michael Pante (michael.pante@colostate.edu) with questions. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    },
    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/Assistant-Professor_R2026108012-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nJob Description Position Summary: The Department of Psychology at Colorado State University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor in COGNITIVE PSYCHOLOGY with an appointment date of August 16, 2027.  Work authorization visa sponsorship may be available based on the specific situation, including cost, for the selected final candidate.   Priority will be given to candidates with research expertise in areas related to the Science of Learning, Human Factors Psychology, and/or Artificial Intelligence (AI). Candidates should demonstrate the ability to teach undergraduate and graduate level coursework in Cognitive Psychology.   The Department of Psychology is part of the College of Natural Sciences and serves approximately 1,600 undergraduate majors and 100 graduate students. Faculty are distributed across five doctoral programs: 1. Cognitive Psychology 2. Cognitive Neuroscience 3. Clinical Psychology 4. Health Psychology 5. Industrial/Organizational Psychology Our department houses state-of-the-art research and clinical facilities, including the Behavioral Sciences Building (LEED Gold Certified), which offers modern classrooms, research labs, and collaborative spaces. Adjacent facilities include department-operated EEG, TMS, and fNIRS labs, and there is access to fMRI facilities with a 15-minute walk of the Behavioral Sciences Building. To ensure full consideration, materials must be received by Monday, November 2, 2026 at 11:59pm, MST. Essential Job Duties: Teach and mentor students at the undergraduate and graduate levels in Psychology, including course and curriculum development. Conduct and publish research, pursue external funding, and contribute to scholarly advancement in the field of Cognitive Psychology. Provide service to the department, university, profession, and community in support of CSU’s mission.   Conditions of Employment: Pre-employment background check required (for all new hires).   Supervision: There are no formal supervisory responsibilities for this position.   Minimum Qualifications: Terminal degree (Ph.D. or equivalent) or anticipated completion by 7/31/2027 in the relevant discipline of Cognitive Psychology or a related discipline. Evidence of research productivity or strong potential to establish a sustainable scholarly program (e.g., publications, grant activity) in the area of Cognitive Psychology as demonstrated by a consistent record of publication in Cognitive Psychology. Demonstrated ability to teach effectively at the undergraduate and/or graduate level in the area of Cognitive Psychology and related courses, commensurate with their educational/career stage (e.g., time since completing the doctorate), indicated in the teaching statement.   Preferred Qualifications: A sustained research program related to the 3 targeted areas for growth within Cognitive Psychology at CSU: i) Science of Learning (e.g., basic and applied research in human memory, learning, attention, reasoning, problem solving or creativity), ii) Human Factors Psychology (e.g., applied attention theory, attentional focus in a multimedia environment, decision and risk, cybersecurity, human-AI interaction) or iii) Artificial Intelligence (e.g., human-AI interaction, the study of Large Language Models (LLMs), the study of AI in education, the application of cognitive science for improving AI design and implementation, machine learning approaches to understanding cognition such as Natural Language Processing, Learning Analytics for applying Cognitive Psychology in educational settings, AI-enhanced learning, computational models of cognition, increasingly human-like AI systems). A sustained record of publication in Q1-Q2 journals in Cognitive Psychology or closely related fields. A record of collaboration or demonstrated potential for collaboration with colleagues in related fields. Demonstrated excellence in teaching at the undergraduate and possibly at the graduate level commensurate with their educational/career stage in Cognitive Psychology and related courses (e.g., Science of Learning, Learning and Memory, Human Factors, Applied Cognition, Sensation and Perception, Research Methods or courses related to Data Science). A record of mentoring undergraduate and possibly graduate students commensurate with educational/career stage in Cognitive Psychology. A sustained record of applying for and potentially obtaining external research funding, commensurate with their educational/career stage. Expertise to contribute to AI uses, implementations, and understanding as a targeted area of growth at CSU. Application Instructions: To apply, please upload one single PDF file no more than 5MB containing all required application materials below in the order provided. Cover Letter CV Statement of research interests Teaching statement If you advance to the semi-finalist stage, you will receive an e-mail with instructions to provide the contact information for three professional references. Once you submit your references' contact information, each reference will receive an e-mail with instructions for submitting a letter of recommendation. We will notify you with the deadline of when letters should be submitted at this stage in the hiring process. Please note, for semi-finalist candidates, submitted letters of recommendation, along with application materials, will be made available to the Psychology Department faculty for review. Please direct questions about the application process to Ginger Lacy-Gill at ginger.lacy-gill@colostate.edu. Salary Range $83,000-87,000 Required Application Documents To apply, please upload the following applicant documents. Ensure your materials fully address the required and preferred job qualifications of the position. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Cover Letter, Resume/CV, Statement of Teaching/Research Philosophy Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    },
    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/fortcollins_careers/job/Fort-Collins-CO/Instructor--Health-and-Exercise-Science_R2026108098": {
      "title": "Instructor, Health and Exercise Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nJob Description Position Summary: The Department of Health and Exercise Science seeks full-time, 9-month, non-tenure-track faculty to support undergraduate teaching and experiential learning. Responsibilities include contributing to instruction in areas such as exercise physiology, human physiology, and pathophysiology, supporting the coordination and administration of undergraduate practicum, internship, and other applied learning experiences. The position will work closely with students and clinical, fitness, healthcare, and community partners to facilitate high-quality professional experiences and strengthen connections between academic preparation and career readiness. Instructors will also contribute meaningful service to the department, college, and university. Faculty in the Department of Health and Exercise Science teach and conduct research in state-of-the-art facilities, with an emphasis on preparing students to help people protect, maintain, and improve their health and quality of life. To learn more, please visit https://www.chhs.colostate.edu/hes/ . For full consideration, applications must be received by 11:59 p.m. MT on November 30, 2026. Essential Duties: Teach assigned undergraduate and graduate courses or sections in exercise physiology, human physiology, pathophysiology, and related areas.  Coordinate with other instructors to maintain consistent course content, learning outcomes, instructional materials, and student expectations across multi-section courses. Develop syllabi, course materials, assessments, and other instructional resources and provide regular student office hours.  Advise and support students regarding academic planning, careers, and professional opportunities in healthcare, fitness, and related fields.  Develop and maintain relationships with industry, healthcare providers, and other partners to support applied learning and experiential opportunities for students.  Participate in departmental committees, student-oriented events, outreach activities, and other service activities that support the department and its students.    Supervision: None  Conditions of Employment:   Pre-employment Criminal Background Check (required for new hires).  Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree (or Ed.D.) in health and exercise science, kinesiology, exercise physiology, physiology, or a closely related field.   Experience in college- or university-level undergraduate teaching experience or similar.  Experience developing course curricula and academic support materials. Preferred Qualifications: Experience coordinating or administering undergraduate practicum, internship, or other experiential-learning programs in health and exercise science, kinesiology, or related discipline.   Demonstrated experience developing relationships with clinical, fitness, healthcare, or community partners and mentoring students through applied professional experiences.  Experience with instruction of exercise physiology at the undergraduate level.  Experience with instruction of pathophysiology at the undergraduate level.  Application Instructions: To apply, please upload all the following required application material in the Resume/Cover Letter section of the application: Cover Letter and Resume/CV (combined single PDF file preferred) Personal Teaching Philosophy Salary Range $65,000 - 80,000 Required Application Documents To apply, please upload the following applicant documents. Ensure your materials fully address the required and preferred job qualifications of the position. Please note, applicants may redact information from their application materials that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution. Cover Letter, Resume/CV, Statement of Teaching/Research Philosophy Employee Benefits Colorado State University is not just a workplace; it’s a thriving community that’s transforming lives and improving the human condition through world-class teaching, research, and service. With a robust benefits package, collaborative atmosphere, and focus on work-life balance, CSU is where you can thrive, grow, and make a lasting impact. Review our detailed benefits information here. Explore the additional perks of working at CSU here. For the total value of CSU benefits in addition to wages, use our compensation calculator. Lastly, click here for more information about why Fort Collins is consistently ranked in the top cities to live in! Background Check Policy Statement Colorado State University strives to provide a safe study, work, and living environment for its faculty, staff, volunteers and students. To support this environment and comply with applicable laws and regulations, CSU conducts background checks for the finalist before a final offer. The type of background check conducted varies by position and can include, but is not limited to, criminal history, sex offender registry, motor vehicle history, financial history, and/or education verification. Background checks will also be conducted when required by law or contract and when, in the discretion of the University, it is reasonable and prudent to do so. EEO Colorado State University (CSU) provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws."
    }
